# Advanced settings for MiMo-V2.6-Flash-RL on four CMP 170HX cards.
#
# You almost certainly don't need anything here: the common settings are in
# .env.example. ./start.sh reads only .env, so to use a setting from this
# file, copy its line into your .env (not into this file) and uncomment it.
# Every line shows the default the scripts use when it is unset, so a later
# release's new defaults reach you on ./start.sh update without editing .env.
# Delete or re-comment a line to go back to the default. The paths
# (/path/to/...) and HF_TOKEN lines are placeholders, not defaults; the note
# above each says what the default is.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, notes on their own lines starting with #.
# An unquoted value ends at the first " #" (whitespace then #), and a trailing
# "  (...)" (two or more spaces, then a note in parentheses) is dropped too.
# Quote the value, "..." or '...', to keep everything between the quotes.
# A prefix env assignment overrides .env for every key, including an
# explicit empty (KEY=):   MAX_SEQS=16 ./start.sh restart
#
# === paths ==============================================================
# Give an ABSOLUTE path when you move one. MODELS_DIR is in .env.example.
# Default: MODELS_DIR/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-RL-NVFP4. The DFlash drafter is its dflash/ folder.
# MODEL=/path/to/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-RL-NVFP4
#
# Weights to download: the repository and the pinned revision. The gguf/ folder
# (another copy of the weights for other engines) is excluded.
# TARGET_REPO=ProCreations/MiMo-V2.6-Flash-RL-NVFP4
# TARGET_REVISION=34cebc5d75743a93ab76145ec609cfef9da8c417
# Unauthenticated Hub downloads are rate limited; a token is faster.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx
# 1 re-fetches the weights even when the files are already there.
# REFRESH_WEIGHTS=0
# === serving limits =====================================================
# Context length in tokens, up to the model's 1,048,576. Lowering it does not
# free memory: the KV cache is a fixed byte budget (KV_MEM), not a function of
# the context.
# MAX_LEN=1048576
# KV cache per card, in bytes. 10 GiB holds about 1.64 M tokens at bf16 KV.
# KV_MEM=10737418240
# KV cache precision: bfloat16, or fp8_e4m3 (twice the tokens per byte; not
# with SPEC_MODE=dflash, whose drafter has no fp8 KV path on sm_80).
# KV_DTYPE=bfloat16
# Concurrent sequences.
# MAX_SEQS=32
# Tokens per scheduler step (the prefill chunk). Bigger reads prompts faster
# and costs KV pool, since each sliding-window layer reserves in-flight tokens
# per request: measured 1,024 -> 1,643,784 tokens and 2,471 tok/s cold prefill;
# 2,048 -> 1,615,953 and 2,728; 4,096 -> 1,563,025 and 2,859.
# MAX_BATCHED=2048
# Fair prefill: while anyone is decoding, prompts are read in slices of this
# many tokens so decoders keep getting steps; 0 turns it off. A 30K prompt
# landing mid-answer: decoder 10 tok/s at 0, 15 at 384, 36 at 128; the
# prompt's own read takes 20 % / 65 % longer (docs/results.md).
# FAIR_CHUNK=384
# Prompts that may be mid-read at once with FAIR_CHUNK on.
# FAIR_PARTIAL=2
# Parsers for MiMo's reasoning blocks and tool calls.
# REASONING_PARSER=mimo
# TOOL_PARSER=mimo
# Extra vLLM arguments, whitespace-separated. Options that change the
# deployment (parallelism, dtype, context, graphs, speculation) are refused.
# EXTRA_ARGS=
# Seconds to wait for /health after launch.
# READY_TIMEOUT=1800
# 1 runs the post-start check (two requests, drafting active) after health.
# Set 0 with SPEC_MODE=none: the check expects drafting.
# BOOT_CHECK=1
# Seconds stop waits for a clean shutdown.
# STOP_TIMEOUT=120
# === speculative decoding ===============================================
# SPEC_MODE is in .env.example: dflash, mtp or none.
# Draft tokens per step. Default 7 for dflash (1..8: the drafter's block is 8
# wide), 2 for mtp.
# SPEC_N=
# Drafts by batch size: a JSON list of [first_batch,last_batch,drafts] ranges
# without spaces from batch 1, e.g. [[1,2,7],[3,32,4]]. Empty gives dflash the
# default schedule, 7 drafts for one request, 5 for two, 3 from three up to
# MAX_SEQS (docs/results.md: +11 % structured and +39 % prose at eight users
# against a fixed 7); mtp gets none. none: SPEC_N at every batch size. SPEC_N
# caps every entry.
# SPEC_SCHEDULE=
# The engine's adaptive draft depth (its SpeculativeConfig.adaptive_k), a JSON
# object without spaces; by_load entry i is the depth for i+1 requests, accept
# weighs recent acceptance. Measured mixed: prose up, structured output down.
# SPEC_ADAPTIVE_K=
# === KV offload =========================================================
# Host RAM, in GiB, that keeps KV blocks evicted from the cards and copies
# them back instead of re-prefilling (vLLM's OffloadingConnector). 0: off.
# The tier lives in the container's /dev/shm, so the default SHM_SIZE grows
# to KV_OFFLOAD_GB + 32 GiB. About 24 KB per token: 64 GiB holds about 2.7 M tokens.
# KV_OFFLOAD_GB=0
# A directory for a disk tier behind the RAM tier (needs KV_OFFLOAD_GB).
# Write-through, never pruned by the engine: size the disk and prune it
# yourself. See docs/results.md for what it does to reloads.
# KV_OFFLOAD_DIR=/path/to/kvtier
# === parallelism ========================================================
# 1 keeps whole routed experts on each card (vLLM --enable-expert-parallel);
# measured 4-9 % slower than the default slicing on these cards.
# EXPERT_PARALLEL=0
# === vision patch =======================================================
# 0 runs the engine's own mimo_v2_omni.py instead of patches/ (images misread).
# VISION_PATCH=1
# === CUDA graphs ========================================================
# FULL_AND_PIECEWISE (default: the whole decode step as one graph) or PIECEWISE.
# GRAPH_MODE=FULL_AND_PIECEWISE
# === container ==========================================================
# CONTAINER_NAME=mimo-v26-flash
# Default 32g, or KV_OFFLOAD_GB + 32 GiB with the RAM tier on.
# SHM_SIZE=32g
# Default: cache/ in this repo.
# CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache
# === preflight ==========================================================
# Preflight limits (read only).
# MIN_GPUS=4
# MIN_GPU_MIB=61440
# NEED_DISK_GB=190
# === engine switches (kill switches: set 0 and restart) =================
# Flags-in-data two-shot custom all-reduce for the TP4 all-reduces it covers.
# VLLM_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE_FLAGS=1
# Custom all-reduce over PCIe peer access (applies only after the P2P check passes).
# VLLM_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE_PCIE_P2P=1
# NCCL over peer access (applies only after the P2P check passes).
# NCCL_P2P_LEVEL=SYS
# Allocator: custom all-reduce needs legacy CUDA IPC handles.
# PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:False
# Worker start method.
# VLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD=spawn
